# Test select-once with lazy send: sent: [send ch1 42] is never forced
# (only .result is accessed, which accesses result which calls select-once).
# The send thunk is never materialized, so ch1 has no value.
# select-once polls all channels up to MAX_SELECT_POLLS times, finds nothing,
# and raises a resource limit error (E043).
--- uses: ["core"]
[
  ch1: [channel 5]
  ch2: [channel 5]
  sent: [send ch1 42]
  pair1: [ch: ch1  handler: [fn [let x] [str "ch1:" x]]]
  pair2: [ch: ch2  handler: [fn [let x] [str "ch2:" x]]]
  sources: [seq pair1 [seq pair2 Seq.End]]
  result: [select-once [context] sources]
]
.result
=== error
[E043] select-once: channel poll limit exceeded — no channel was ready (defined at 13:11-13:42) (called at 6:1-15:8)
  in [select-once ...] at 13:11-13:42
